          "Beach Train (Mipo to Songjeong, 4.8 km, 7 stops): 10,000 single from an end station, 8,000 from Cheongsapo, 16,000 for the all-stations pass. October hours are 09:00-19:30 for the train and 08:30-18:30 for the capsule.",
          "Sky Capsule weekend slots sell out. Book on bluelinepark.com (may need Korean phone verification) or on Klook/KKday as soon as the date opens; weekdays are easiest.",
          "Gwangalli drone show (about 1,100 drones, free) runs Saturdays at 19:00 and 21:00 in October. Oct 24 2026 is 'Forest's Melody' and is the only realistic date, which argues for putting Busan around Oct 21-24 and taking the KTX plus AREX to ICN on Sun Oct 25.",
          "Hurshimchung (Dongnae hot springs, about 40 baths) reopened on 1 May 2026 after renovation: 15,000 weekday / 18,000 weekend, 05:30-22:00, open daily.",
          "Spa Land Centum is still open in 2026, but hours changed on 1 Sep 2026 to 09:00-22:00, and the price is a flat 26,000 KRW with a 4-hour limit.",
          "Haeundae Grand Hotel is closed (since 2018/19) and is being redeveloped. Remove it from the shortlist.",
          "The most onsen-ryokan-like stays are Paradise Hotel Busan (Cimer outdoor sea-view hot spring; about 350-650k KRW per night for 3), Ananti Cove (Water House, clifftop; about 350-700k), and the budget option Hotel Nongshim (triple ondol room plus Hurshimchung, about 180-300k, no sea view).",
          "Huinnyeoul Culture Village on Yeongdo plus the Sky Capsule/Cheongsapo stretch give the closest Kamakura/Enoden feel; Haedong Yonggungsa is the seaside-temple analog (free, go at sunrise).",
          "Autumn: Busan mountain foliage peaks mid to late November, so late October is mostly green. Seunghaksan silver grass peaks mid-Oct to early Nov (good); Daejeo pink muhly is fading by Oct 20; Tongyeong oyster season opens in October.",
          "Festivals: Dongnae Eupseong History Festival and Jeonpo Coffee Festival are Oct 16-18; Busan Folk Arts Festival is Oct 24-25; Jagalchi Festival 2026 dates are unconfirmed (2025 was Oct 23-26). BIFF (Oct 6-15) and the Busan Fireworks (Nov 7) fall outside the trip.",
          "Songdo cable car (verified): 19,000 standard / 24,000 glass-floor round trip, 09:00-21:00 in October."
        ],
