          "The exchange rate on Oct 6-7 2026 is about 1,340 KRW per USD, so US$1,000 per person is about 1,340,000 KRW and the US$3,000 group budget is about 4.02M KRW.",
          "On Sep 1 2026 SRT merged into KTX. Fares on high-speed routes dropped about 10% (Seoul-Busan went from 59,800 to 54,400 KRW), all bookings moved to the Korail+ app (formerly Korail Talk), and the SRT app is gone.",
          "Since Oct 1 2026, Korail tickets open 2 months ahead at 07:00, so every train for Oct 17-25 is already on sale. Book now, especially weekend trains and the Donghae Line, which runs only 3 trains a day.",
          "October 2026 timetable fares per person: Seoul to Gyeongju (formerly Singyeongju) 44,500 KRW, about 2h. Gyeongju to Busan 10,100 KRW, about 30 min. Seoul to Gangneung 27,600 KRW, about 2h. Seoul to Jeonju 31,900 KRW. Cheongnyangni to Andong 27,700 KRW, 1h52.",
          "East-coast KTX-Eum: Bujeon to Gangneung costs 46,800 KRW and takes 3h50, with only 3 trains a day (07:50/13:58/19:40). Gangneung to Gyeongju is 34,300 KRW, 2h50. Gangneung to Pohang is 28,700 KRW, 2h22. Bujeon to Gyeongju is 12,500 KRW, 1h07.",
          "The Korail Pass is not worth it. A Seoul to Gyeongju to Busan to Seoul loop costs about 109,000 KRW per person, against 131,000-275,000 KRW for a pass. It is also officially unclear whether the pass covers former SRT trains.",
          "Express and intercity bus fare caps rose 9% on Oct 1 2026. Seoul-Sokcho (about 21,000-26,000 KRW, 2h10-2h40) and Gangneung-Sokcho (about 8,500 KRW, 1h) are estimates.",
          "Dawn arrival: the AREX Express first train leaves T1 at 05:23 (11,000-13,000 KRW, 43 min). For 3 people a taxi (about 65,000-80,000 KRW total) costs about the same and goes door to door. The safest plan is to book a room for the night of Oct 16.",
          "Air Premia is believed to use ICN T1 (confirm). Air Premia is not among the Seoul Station City Airport Terminal check-in airlines, so the last day needs hotel bag storage or T-Luggage (stations 09:00-22:00; airport delivery 20,000 KRW weekday / 29,000 KRW weekend per bag).",
          "Entry: US citizens are exempt from K-ETA through Dec 31 2026. Each traveler must file the free e-Arrival Card online within 3 days before arrival (it replaced paper cards on Jan 1 2026).",
          "Payments: foreign Visa/MC work almost everywhere. For transit, use T-money or WOWPASS. Kakao T, k.ride and Uber work with foreign cards. Use Naver/Kakao Map rather than Google, and CatchTable Global for omakase bookings.",
          "Overseas cards sometimes fail 3-D Secure on Korail+. Fall back to the korail.com English site, station counters, or resellers (Trip.com, Klook, LACHA)."
