        "headline_findings": [
          "Best Kamakura analog: Busan's east coast. That means the Blueline Park Sky Capsule and Beach Train between Mipo, Cheongsapo and Songjeong, then Haedong Yonggungsa, Cheongsapo and Huinnyeoul. Yangyang Naksansa with Sokcho's Abai Village ranks 2nd, then Gangneung, Tongyeong, Yeosu and Seogwipo.",
          "Official 2026 Blueline fares: a 3-person Sky Capsule costs KRW 55,000 one way (KRW 18,300 per person). The Beach Train is KRW 8,000-10,000 one way, or KRW 16,000 for a day pass. In October the Sky Capsule runs 08:30-18:30, about 30 minutes each way, and weekend slots sell out.",
          "Best Shibuya analogs, in order: Hongdae/Yeonnam (street energy), Myeongdong with Euljiro Nogari Alley, Seongsu (more like Daikanyama), Gangnam Station (the literal big crossing), and Busan Seomyeon.",
          "Korea has almost no all-in-one ryokans. The closest is Gyeongju Ragung, a hanok hotel with private outdoor stone baths, but its domain ragung.co.kr no longer resolves. Treat its operating status as unverified.",
          "Practical ryokan substitute: an ocean-view hot-spring hotel (Paradise Hotel Busan's Cimer spa, or Ananti Cove's Water House) plus a kaiseki-like dinner. Mori in Busan, a 1-star Japanese kaiseki run by a Korean chef and his Japanese wife, is the closest match.",
          "Michelin Seoul & Busan 2026 (announced Mar 5, 2026): 46 starred restaurants. Mingles is the only 3-star. Sosuheon is the only 2-star sushi counter (new). Sushi Matsumoto and Sushi Kanesaka (new) hold 1 star. Busan has 4 one-star restaurants, including Mori and Le DORER (new).",
          "Sushi Kanesaka Seoul (InterContinental Parnas) official 2026 prices: lunch KRW 230,000-280,000, dinner KRW 330,000-380,000. It has 9 seats and books by phone at 02-559-7627.",
          "Sosuheon: an 8-seat hanok counter with dinner around KRW 500,000. It books by phone only (+82 10-9694-3368).",
          "Hanu omakase: Born and Bred in Majang-dong (No. 56 on Asia's 50 Best Restaurants 2026). Its chef's tasting costs KRW 380,000 and books on CatchTable 2-3 months ahead. The restaurant is closed Tuesdays.",
          "Mingles raised its lunch to KRW 320,000 on Mar 1, 2026, and is closed Sun-Mon. Onjium serves Joseon court cuisine opposite Gyeongbokgung at lunch only, Tue-Fri (per Michelin). Michelin lists it as cash only.",
          "October seafood: gizzard shad (jeoneo), daeha prawns and kkotge crab are in season. Oysters are just starting in Tongyeong, and Yangyang pine mushrooms run until about mid-October. Domestic snow crab (daegae) is NOT in season in October; what you see is imported or red snow crab.",
          "Hoe (raw fish) markets: Jagalchi platters run about KRW 30,000-60,000 for two, plus about KRW 5,000 per person for the table. Millak, facing Gwangan Bridge, is the best night out. Noryangjin wholesale flatfish was KRW 22,800/kg in Aug 2026."
        ],
